The MIT licence above covers the source code in this repository.

It does NOT cover the data the application downloads at build time, nor the flight log it ships.
Those carry their own licences and attribution requirements, which are listed in NOTICE.md and must
travel with any redistribution or public deployment.

In particular:

  * the 1 m terrain and the LoD2 buildings are Bayerische Vermessungsverwaltung open data under
    CC BY 4.0 — free to reuse, on condition that the prescribed notice is shown;
  * the coarse terrain shell is Copernicus DEM, under the Copernicus DEM open licence;
  * land cover, the transport network and the cableway come from OpenStreetMap under the ODbL;

none of which are ours to relicense. The attribution block in NOTICE.md is rendered in the
application footer, and an end-to-end test asserts it is present — dropping it from a deployment is
a licence breach rather than a cosmetic regression.
